      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, you've just stumbled onto the classic goblin debt trap—the kind that keeps a goblin's treasure chest full while you're left with a lighter purse. Your monthly payment is like a fixed ration of bread for a starving goblin: it goes to the most urgent need first, which is the interest, not the principal.  \n\nHere's the sneaky bit: interest accrues daily on your current balance, so early on, a huge chunk of your payment just covers that interest. Only the leftover crumbs actually chip away at the principal. As the principal shrinks, the interest gets smaller, so more of your payment goes to the principal—but that takes time, like a goblin slowly digging a tunnel.  \n\nIf you want to speed it up, you can pay extra toward the principal specifically, or ask your lender to apply any overpayment that way. Otherwise, you're just feeding the interest goblin first, every single month.",
